    "introduction": "Burberry designs and sells luxury clothing, accessories and related products under its British heritage brand. Its offering includes outerwear, leather goods and fashion collections distributed through directly operated stores, online channels and wholesale partners, with licensing in selected categories. Revenue depends on customer demand, pricing and the mix of products sold. Brand identity, design and retail presentation are central to its positioning, while controlling distribution helps shape the customer experience. Luxury spending can vary with tourism, consumer confidence and regional economic conditions. Inventory management and the cost of stores and marketing influence profitability, making both creative direction and retail execution important.",
